$ whycant --all -u www-data read '/srv/up/a
b.txt'

✗ www-data (uid 33) cannot read /srv/up/a\nb.txt

  /                  drwxr-xr-x  root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv               drwxr-xr-x  root:root      ✓ traverse
  /srv/up            drwxr-x---  deploy:deploy  ✗ traverse   ← blocked here
  /srv/up/a\nb.txt   -rw-r-----  deploy:deploy  ✗ read   ← blocked here

Why
  /srv/up: other class has no execute permission
    www-data is not the owner (deploy) and is not in group "deploy",
    so the "other" permissions apply: ---. Entering a directory needs x.

  /srv/up/a\nb.txt: other class has no read permission
    www-data is not the owner (deploy) and is not in group "deploy",
    so the "other" permissions apply: ---. Reading a file needs r.

Fixes (safest first, for each problem)
  /srv/up:
  1. Grant traverse only to www-data via ACL:
       sudo setfacl -m u:www-data:x /srv/up
  2. Add www-data to the deploy group (restart the service afterwards):
       sudo usermod -aG deploy www-data
  /srv/up/a\nb.txt:
  3. Grant read access only to www-data via ACL:
       sudo setfacl -m u:www-data:r $'/srv/up/a\nb.txt'
